{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ARIMAModel","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SARIMAModel","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/TimeSeriesMetrics"],"anchor":"Forecasting-Models","title":"Forecasting Models"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Time series observations often display temporal autocorrelation, stochastic drift, and repetitive seasonal cycles. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftForecast"},{"type":"text","text":" provides high-performance, actor-isolated statistical models optimized with Apple Accelerate SIMD linear algebra:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ARIMAModel","type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Models non-seasonal series using $(p, d, q)$ specifications with vectorized two-stage Hannan-Rissanen conditional least-squares parameter estimation."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SARIMAModel","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Extends ARIMA to capture multiplicative seasonal cycles $(p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s$ via polynomial cross-term refinement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Performs parallelized grid search over potential order permutations, selecting optimal configurations via AIC or BIC criteria.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"code":["graph TD","    RawSeries[Raw Time Series Y_t] --> StationarityCheck{Requires Differencing?}","    StationarityCheck -->|Yes| Diff[Differencing: d order \/ Seasonal D order]","    StationarityCheck -->|No| ModelChoice{Model Selection}","    Diff --> ModelChoice","    ModelChoice -->|Manual Specification| FitARIMA[ARIMAModel \/ SARIMAModel]","    ModelChoice -->|Automated Grid Search| Auto[AutoARIMA Task Group]","    Auto --> BestOrder[Optimal Order via AIC\/BIC]","    BestOrder --> FitARIMA","    FitARIMA --> ForecastResult[ARIMAResult: Point Forecasts + Confidence Intervals]","    ForecastResult --> WAPE[WAPE \/ sMAPE Evaluation]"],"syntax":"mermaid","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"1. Non-Seasonal ARIMA Modeling","anchor":"1-Non-Seasonal-ARIMA-Modeling","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An $\\text{ARIMA}(p, d, q)$ model combines:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"$p$ (Autoregressive Order)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Dependence on preceding $p$ lagged values."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"$d$ (Differencing Order)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Degree of differencing required to achieve weak stationarity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"$q$ (Moving Average Order)","type":"text"}]},{"text":": Dependence on preceding $q$ white-noise forecast errors.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Fitting and Multi-Step Forecasting","level":3,"anchor":"Fitting-and-Multi-Step-Forecasting","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize historical series (e.g., monthly sales)","let monthlySales: [Double] = [","    112, 118, 132, 129, 121, 135, 148, 148, 136, 119, 104, 118,","    115, 126, 141, 135, 125, 149, 170, 170, 158, 133, 114, 140","]","","\/\/ 2. Initialize actor-isolated ARIMA(1, 1, 1) model","let arima = try ARIMAModel(p: 1, d: 1, q: 1)","","\/\/ 3. Fit parameters via Hannan-Rissanen conditional least-squares","try await arima.fit(series: monthlySales)","","\/\/ 4. Generate out-of-sample forecast for next 6 horizons","let result = try await arima.forecast(horizon: 6)","","print(\"Point Forecasts: \\(result.pointForecasts)\")","if let lower = result.lowerConfidenceInterval, let upper = result.upperConfidenceInterval {","    for i in 0..<result.pointForecasts.count {","        print(\"t+\\(i + 1): \\(String(format: \"%.1f\", result.pointForecasts[i])) [95% CI: \\(String(format: \"%.1f\", lower[i])) – \\(String(format: \"%.1f\", upper[i]))]\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"2. Seasonal SARIMA Modeling","anchor":"2-Seasonal-SARIMA-Modeling","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When data exhibits recurring seasonal patterns (such as quarterly retail spikes or 24-hour diurnal rhythms), standard non-seasonal differencing is insufficient."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SARIMAModel","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" incorporates multiplicative seasonal operators:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"$$(p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s$$","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"where:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"$s$","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Seasonal period length ($s=4$ for quarterly, $s=12$ for monthly, $s=7$ for daily data).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"$P, D, Q$"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Seasonal autoregressive, seasonal differencing, and seasonal moving-average orders."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ Initialize SARIMA(1, 1, 1) x (1, 1, 0)_12 for monthly seasonal data","let sarima = try SARIMAModel(","    p: 1, d: 1, q: 1,","    P: 1, D: 1, Q: 0,","    s: 12",")","","try await sarima.fit(series: monthlySales)","","\/\/ Forecast 12 months ahead","let seasonalForecast = try await sarima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"12-Month Ahead Forecast: \\(seasonalForecast.pointForecasts)\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. Automated Order Selection (`AutoARIMA`)","anchor":"3-Automated-Order-Selection-AutoARIMA"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Determining optimal $(p, d, q)$ and $(P, D, Q)_s$ orders manually through autocorrelation (ACF) and partial autocorrelation (PACF) plots can be labor-intensive. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA"},{"text":" evaluates an exhaustive or bounded grid concurrently across Apple Silicon CPU cores, penalizing complexity with AIC or BIC:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ Initialize automated grid search engine","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    seasonal: true,","    seasonalPeriod: 12,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ Search across candidate permutations","let searchResult = try await autoArima.fit(series: monthlySales)","","print(\"Selected Optimal Order: \\(searchResult.bestOrder)\")","\/\/ Example: SARIMA(1, 1, 1)(0, 1, 1)[12]","print(\"Optimal AIC Score: \\(searchResult.bestScore)\")","","\/\/ Forecast directly using the winning model","let bestForecast = try await searchResult.forecast(horizon: 6)","print(\"Best Forecast: \\(bestForecast.pointForecasts)\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"4-Forecasting-Accuracy-with-TimeSeriesMetrics","text":"4. Forecasting Accuracy with `TimeSeriesMetrics`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Validate predictions against holdout test folds using standard metric evaluators, including Weighted Absolute Percentage Error (WAPE):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","let actuals: [Double] = [150.0, 162.0, 180.0, 175.0, 160.0, 142.0]","let predictions = result.pointForecasts","","let wapeError = TimeSeriesMetrics.wape(actual: actuals, forecast: predictions)","let smapeError = TimeSeriesMetrics.smape(actual: actuals, forecast: predictions)","let rmseError = TimeSeriesMetrics.rmse(actual: actuals, forecast: predictions)","","print(\"WAPE: \\(String(format: \"%.2f%%\", wapeError * 100))\")","print(\"sMAPE: \\(String(format: \"%.2f%%\", smapeError * 100))\")","print(\"RMSE: \\(String(format: \"%.2f\", rmseError))\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"ARIMA & SARIMA Time Series Models"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Forecast univariate time series with trends and periodic seasonalities using Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA), Seasonal ARIMA (SARIMA), and Automated Order Selection (AutoARIMA)."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimaandsarima"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/SARIMAModel":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Seasonal AutoRegressive Integrated Moving Average (SARIMA) time-series forecasting model actor."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SARIMAModel","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/sarimamodel","title":"SARIMAModel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SARIMAModel","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SARIMAModel","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/ARIMAModel":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ARIMAModel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ARIMAModel","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ARIMAModel"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"AutoRegressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA) time-series forecasting model actor.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimamodel","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ARIMAModel"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAParallel":{"role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel","type":"topic","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","kind":"article"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftForecast","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast","abstract":[{"text":"Time Series & Volatility Forecasting Models.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/SmoothingAndDecomposition":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/smoothinganddecomposition","title":"Time Series Forecasting, Smoothing & Kalman Filtering","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","abstract":[{"text":"Model trends, seasonality, volatility, and dynamic state transitions using ","type":"text"},{"code":"ExponentialSmoothing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"NelderMead","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KalmanFilter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"GARCHModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeSeriesDecomposition"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/KoopmanOperator":{"title":"KoopmanOperator","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/koopmanoperator","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KoopmanOperator","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Koopman Operator time-series forecasting and dynamical system modeling actor.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Uses Extended Dynamic Mode Decomposition (EDMD) to approximate non-linear dynamics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"via linear operators in lifted observable feature spaces.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KoopmanOperator","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAOrder":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A structure identifying the selected ARIMA \/ SARIMA order."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaorder","title":"AutoARIMAOrder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMA":{"title":"AutoARIMA","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMA"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Automated hyperparameter grid search for ARIMA and SARIMA time-series models.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarima","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMA"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/TimeSeriesMetrics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Canonical evaluation metrics for time-series forecasting and out-of-sample validation (G-020).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/TimeSeriesMetrics","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/timeseriesmetrics","title":"TimeSeriesMetrics","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeSeriesMetrics","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeSeriesMetrics","kind":"identifier"}]}}}